Negative control for the DECLARATION supplying the default visible set
(`R6-25` · `R6-35`).

Boots the table on its first declared column alone and leaves the rest for the
user to switch on. Every other law still holds — the picker offers all of them,
the url still carries the set, the order is still the declaration's — so what is
on trial is only the claim that the table uischema IS the default: a page that
lands showing one column has silently made the declaration a menu rather than a
table.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the column-set spec — with no `columns=` in the url the header row draws
one column instead of every declared one, so the default-set cases fail while
the round-trip cases still pass.

